{# NEEDS ATTENTION — sorted by urgency, never by module.

   BOUNDED, LIKE EVERY LIST IN A CARD. The list is as long as the modules'
   day: thirty-four items made this card two thousand pixels tall and pushed
   the ground off the screen. So the card draws the most urgent few and says
   what it is drawing them out of, with the way to all of them — the overflow
   ruling, which every card on every surface keeps. #}
{% set latest = latest|default(6) %}
{# NEEDS ATTENTION — sorted by urgency, never by module. #}
<div class="c">
    {# THE CAPTION CARRIES IT: how many, and whose. Sorted by urgency and never
   by module, and an item leaves when the thing that raised it is dealt with
   — both true, both facts about the card rather than sentences for it, so
   they live here and not in the body. #}
    <span class="tab">Needs attention<span class="src">&middot; {{ attention|length }} item{{ attention|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot; every installed module</span></span>
    <span class="ao-by"><i></i>the area &middot; module items</span>

    {% for item in attention|slice(0, latest) %}
        <a class="ao-att {{ item.severity.cssClass }}" href="{{ item.url }}">
            <span class="sev"></span>
            <span class="bd">
                <span class="t"><b>{{ item.headline }}</b>{% if item.detail %} {{ item.detail }}{% endif %}</span>
                <span class="m"><i></i>{{ item.moduleLabel }} &middot; {{ item.kind }}
                    {%- for fact in item.meta %}<span>{{ fact }}</span>{% endfor -%}
                </span>
            </span>
            <span class="age">{{ item.ageLabel }}</span>
        </a>
    {% else %}
        {# A GOOD DAY IS ALLOWED TO LOOK LIKE ONE. #}
        <p class="zeb">Nothing is asking for attention in this area.
            {% if installedSlugs is empty %}No module is switched on here yet, so nothing is watching.{% endif %}</p>
    {% endfor %}

    {# WHAT THE CARD IS SHOWING, OUT OF WHAT. A bounded list that did not say
       so would read as the whole list on a bad morning. #}
    {% if attention|length > latest %}
        {# THE COUNT, AND NO LINK: there is no page of every item, because an
           item belongs to the module that raised it. Saying "view all" to a
           place that does not exist is worse than saying where they are. #}
        <div class="ao-more">
            <span class="mono">{{ latest }} of {{ attention|length }}</span>
            <span class="sp"></span>
            <span class="mono">the rest are in the modules that raised them</span>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
